**This is money arithmetic and a refusal.** A per-site line prices typed quantity x S (S = the section's sites holding at least one device) and the independent purchase reconciler must agree with it; a quote with no usable site must not price at all and must say so in the product owner's words. Wrong answers a user would meet: a component priced for the wrong number of sites (quote too low or too high, the reconciler agreeing or not), a quote priced when it should be refused (a line costed at 0 sites), or the note shown on the wrong refusal. The product owner's 2026-11-03 rulings, verbatim: "Refuse the quote when a perSite line has no usable sites; count sites with at least one device"; "but make sure there is a note under the entry to indicate the need to the user"; "Build it, strict review (tier 1, as MPSCALC-361)"; the note words: "This line is counted per site. Add a site with at least one device, or the quote cannot be priced." **A price, total, status, hash, id or issue-order change on any existing case, a second string literal, or the note on any refusal but the per-site one, is a Blocker.**
